From 02ade02c15adf79cd2f2032c0666d89301aa4af1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:16:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: starfive: constrain PineTab-V CMA below 4 GiB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The factory VisionFive2-derived U-Boot dynamically resizes the CMA node
after loading a board DTB.  It also attempts to add an alloc-ranges
property that keeps CMA in the low-memory window.  The unpadded PineTab-V
DTB has no room to grow, so that operation fails with FDT_ERR_NOSPACE on
the 8 GiB tablet and Linux places its 1.5 GiB CMA area above 4 GiB.

DC8200 uses a 32-bit DMA mask and cannot address that high CMA area.
Describe U-Boot's low-memory allocation range in the source DT.  U-Boot
can then resize both existing four-cell properties in place for the
detected memory capacity, while a direct kernel boot also keeps CMA in a
DC8200-addressable range.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 .../boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi     | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
index 0b2ae08d6..74d0fa70f 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-pine64-pinetab-v.dtsi
@@ -49,6 +49,7 @@
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reusable;
 			size = <0x0 0x20000000>;
+			alloc-ranges = <0x0 0x70000000 0x0 0x60000000>;
 			alignment = <0x0 0x00400000>;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
